Subject: Name each large grant of the shared graphics memory in the log

The renderer's memory report lists every grant of the shared graphics memory with its process,
size and memory type, but not what the guest made it for, so a 64 MiB grant on SurfaceFlinger's
device could not be traced to the code that asked. The driver's totals line (0016) also left
out the staging grants a device keeps for gralloc buffers' CPU copies (0015).

A grant over 16 MiB (dsa::isLargeGrant) now gets a line of its own when it is made and when it
goes: "dsa-vk large grant: <process> made|let go of <size> of the shared graphics memory, memory
type <n> (<flags>), for <purpose>", where the purpose is an app's host-visible allocation, or a
CPU read back or upload of a <width>x<height> gralloc buffer through the staging grant. The
staging grants now count among the process's grants in the totals line.

Applies after 0018 in patches/guest/mesa, on Mesa 224e91e39836d3ca31f80df2e0379e55c70574f8.
